{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review practices of property management companies and introduce regulation",
        "additional_details": "Property management companies are generally meant to oversee the running of buildings housing apartments where the residents pay service charges to them to do so. I believe one such site in Devon is an example of 100's if not 1000's nationwide (as of May 2026). The ceilings down, an insecure building, badly carried out repairs, no lift, obsolete safety alarms, cannot make contact with company. Bills for services unpaid. Debts run up. Accounts not made available, no transparency, and what I would describe as threatening behaviour. I would like regulation of these companies to improve accountability to be introduced urgently.",
        "background": "I am concerned that nationwide, many elderly and vulnerable people are victims to property management companies' practices. I believe many have extortionate service charges for little in return, and that properties are neglected, unsafe, and unsaleable. Review and regulate these companies.",
